implementationPlan.description:
3. One verification gate, at the end, run once. Run it from the repo root, in place: launcher harnesses run in place per the global rail. Launch it with job control and a scrubbed MOE_*/CLAUDE* env (mem:gotcha-qa-session-env-and-signals-leak-into-harness): `( set -m; nohup bash -c '<command> > log 2>&1; echo EXIT=$? >> log' >/dev/null 2>&1 & )`, then poll the log with a foreground timeout.
The exact command:
`bash -n scripts/moe-agent.sh && bash scripts/tests/parity-check.sh && bash scripts/tests/worktree-landing.sh && bash scripts/tests/postflight-vm-route.sh && MOE_POSTFLIGHT_TIMEOUT_SEC=360 bash scripts/tests/postflight.sh`
Required:
- exit 0;
- parity PASS: MOE_VM_ is not a compared family until CQ-M07n, and no MOE_COMMIT_/MOE_ATTR_/MOE_CHECKPOINT_/MOE_ATTRIBUTION_/MOE_ACCOUNT_ code was added;
- worktree-landing.sh green and unedited, proving legacy worktree completions are unchanged by step 2;
- every [vm candidate] and [strong intent] row passing;
- postflight.sh green, which also re-runs postflight-vm-route.sh through CQ-M07m1's line.
The fresh command, exitCode and outputTail are the complete_task evidence. Load regression-check and verification-before-completion. If a dependency's bytes are missing or a harness cannot run, report that; never claim green.

4. Adversarial self-review, once, scoped to this diff. Load adversarial-self-review. Check each of these:
- a refusal leaves every ref, W's index file and the control checkout byte-identical;
- a set -e trip inside the helper, for example a failed `$(...)` assignment or a missing `contested` file;
- the order is read-tree, then seam, then CAS, then rollback, so an INT/TERM or crash between any two leaves W recoverable by the next pre-flight, never a revert;
- a lost CAS restores W, and a failed rollback still parks NEW;
- no git command writes through the control checkout except rescue_ref_from_commit's refs/moe/rescue ref, and none touches refs/heads/<target>;
- paths with spaces, Unicode or newlines in the staged file;
- the protected seam skip;
- wt_strong_intent cannot pass on stale FROZEN_* from an earlier round or landing (it compares M and B), and it is a no-op for legacy, observe and an empty LAND_TASK_ID;
- no MOE_COMMIT_* code added, so parity holds;
- no shared-mode or legacy worktree behaviour changed.
Size: measure `git diff --numstat -- scripts/`. If it is over 400 net changed lines, file the epic size waiver with moe.propose_rail before complete_task, using the CQ-M05 rail template with the exact per-file numstat (mem:gotcha-cq-plan-size-vs-qa-cap). Re-run step 3's exact command after any fix. Report every created or modified path in complete_step.modifiedFiles. Wrappers own the Git writes: never commit by hand.
